--- Overview
Adds on-disk code signature verification to machutils, so that an executable or bundle can be checked before it is run. Also includes small lifetime and error-handling fixes to the existing requirement code.

--- Key Changes
machutils: file verification
  * Add VerifyFileCodeSignature(path, requirement) and Requirement.VerifyFile(path), which check that code is validly signed, unmodified and satisfies the requirement.
  * Implement the check with SecStaticCodeCheckValidityWithErrors, using strict validation and checking expiration, all architectures and nested code.
  * Add ErrFileCodeSignatureInvalid, returned for unreadable, unsigned, modified or non-matching code. Invalid requirements return ErrInvalidRequirement.
  * Add non-cgo stubs that return ErrCgoDisabled.

machutils: existing requirement code
  * Requirement.Close now clears the finalizer.
  * Requirement.Verify now keeps the requirement alive for the duration of the call using runtime.KeepAlive.
  * verifyGuestCode now initializes outErrMsg to NULL.
  * Move error message extraction into a shared secErrorMessage helper.

Tests and docs
  * Add tests for self-verification, requirement mismatches, modified, unsigned and missing files, Apple binaries and bundles, invalid requirements, and the nil and closed Requirement lifecycle.
  * Extend the non-cgo stub test and update README.md.

